 = A last second opportunity


The Emergency Government is in its last months before elections, yet there's much to be done. We have been hard at work trying to use this chance to try and Target the oligarchs, yet not much can be found besides trails and clues that we simply do not have the time to explore before elections. The fact of the matter is that we need to secure our governance before we can chase these, not to mention the fact that corruption and bias still exists in almost every government institution, something we need to weed out like the oligarchy.

Yet the interior ministry has managed to gain something of interest. Jeppe Bang is a Rogroucean businessman who was a former member of the National Party, and  a part of its parliamentary delegation during the last years of the first republic.  He runs multiple iron mining operations near the Merran border, which were lucky enough to be spared the horrors of war. 

The investigation launched on him found charges of corruption, which is a standard for an oligarch, yet also found evidence of tax evasion that has ran even before the war, perhaps a part of his downfall was his betrayal of his oligarch allies.

The investigation did not take long and a warrent was issued for his arrest, though it seemed like he had the time to sell off most of his assets and was even trying to flee, yet was caught by local police. 

Now we have to get through the slow process of getting him to trial, our progress impeded by non other then the cronies of the Oligarchy. His sold off mines have been closed for a couple months and the miners seem restless. With the economy still recovering, it's hard for them to find work. We need to handle the question of his property fast before this could escalate. 

In the meantime, however,  we can use this time to see what else he is hiding.

-@go

@go
title: A very good development, considering the circumstances..
